# SPARK — local development environment.
#
# ⛔⛔ S182 — READ THIS FIRST: **A `.env` FILE DOES NOT REACH THE BUNDLE FOR ANY KEY LISTED BELOW.**
#
# Measured, not assumed. Put a probe value in `.env`, run `npx vite build`, grep the emitted bundle:
# it appears **0** times. Pass the SAME value as a real environment variable and it appears once.
#
#   VITE_LEADERBOARD_URL=https://probe.example npm run build    # ✅ reaches the bundle
#   echo 'VITE_LEADERBOARD_URL=https://probe.example' > .env    # ❌ silently discarded
#
# WHY: `vite.config.ts` declares every one of these names in its `define` block as
# `JSON.stringify(process.env[k] ?? '')`. Vite loads `.env` into `import.meta.env`, NOT into
# `process.env` — so the define wins and substitutes the empty string. That block exists for a good
# reason (S158 P8: an undeclared key makes CI and local builds differ by bytes and reddens
# `verify-deploy` on every green deploy), and this is its side effect.
#
# ⚠ THIS FILE PREVIOUSLY SAID "copy to .env and fill in", WHICH HAS BEEN FALSE FOR THE THREE TURN
# KEYS SINCE S158. Anyone who followed it got a local build with no relay and nothing to indicate
# why. Found in S182 while wiring the leaderboard; recorded here rather than quietly left in place.
#
# So use this file as a REFERENCE for the names and shapes, and export the values in your shell (or
# prefix the command) when you want them in a local build.
#
# ⛔ `.env` IS GIT-IGNORED AND NONE OF THIS AFFECTS THE LIVE SITE.
#
# The live site at spark-online.space is built by GitHub Actions from a clean checkout, which never
# sees this file. To make a relay reach the DEPLOYED game you must set the same three values as
# repository secrets — see TURN_SETUP.md. This file is for `npm run dev` / a local `npm run build`.

# ─── TURN relay (multiplayer across strict networks) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated. Both a udp and a tcp/443 url is the usual pairing — tcp/443 is what gets through
# restrictive corporate and hotel networks that block everything else.
VITE_TURN_URLS=turn:standard.relay.metered.ca:80,turn:standard.relay.metered.ca:443?transport=tcp
VITE_TURN_USERNAME=
VITE_TURN_CREDENTIAL=

# ─── Shared arcade leaderboard (S182) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Cloudflare Worker origin, and ONLY the origin — the client appends `/board/<id>` itself.
# Must be https on any public host: the live site is HTTPS, so a plain-http endpoint is blocked by
# the browser as mixed content and the board silently falls back to local. http://localhost is fine.
# Unset = the local per-browser board, which is a fully supported state. See
# server/leaderboard/README.md and run `node scripts/leaderboard-wiring-report.mjs` to check a value.
VITE_LEADERBOARD_URL=
